  "baseYear": 2015,
  "note": "Annual average Harmonised Index of Consumer Prices (all-items, COICOP CP00), 2015 = 100. Used to express costs from different price years in comparable real terms. HICP is a consumer-price proxy: a construction cost index (Eurostat sts_copi_a) would be a closer fit and can be substituted without code changes, since src/lib/deflator.ts consumes any table in this shape. USD is the US CPI-U (all urban consumers, all items, US city average), rebased from its native 1982–84 = 100 basis by dividing by the 2015 annual average of 237.017. That is a national CPI, not an HICP. The Serbian series starts in 2006: Eurostat publishes no annual-average HICP index for Serbia before then, and the 1990s hyperinflation and dinar redenomination make splicing the national CPI onto it unsound, so earlier years are absent rather than estimated.",
